INSERT INTO characters (slug,name,team,creator,owner_id,tags,appears_in,data,url_slug,status,updated_at,created_at) VALUES
('peacemonger-scp-fragmented-veil','Peacemonger','townsfolk','legitch',NULL,'','SCP Fragmented Veil','{"slug":"peacemonger-scp-fragmented-veil","name":"Peacemonger","team":"townsfolk","ability":"Each night, choose a player. The 1st time no one died tonight*, you & all chosen teammates are safe from everything until dusk.","creator":"legitch","appearsIn":"SCP Fragmented Veil","lede":"The Peacemonger (SCP-514) are doves that decay all weapons and tools of destruction within their vicinity. They are the embodiments of peace in physical form.","summaryBullets":["The Peacemonger will protect all chosen good players at a time of peace - when no one will die tonight from any ability.","The Peacemonger''s ability will protect players that were chosen when they were good, not all chosen players that are good.","Additionally, the Peacemonger protects against the effects of anything negative, such as Poisoning and Conversion, alongside preventing death for affected players until dusk."],"howToRun":["Each night, wake the Peacemonger and have them choose a player. If they choose a player on their team, put a **HARMONIOUS** reminder token next to that player. Put the Peacemonger to sleep.","Each night except the first, after the Peacemonger has woken and gone to sleep, if no player is to die tonight and the Peacemonger isn''t marked with the **NO ABILITY** reminder, all players marked with the Peacemonger''s **HARMONIOUS** reminder token **are protected from all negative effects, including death, drunkenness, poisoning, or being turned evil** {{i|(see SCP-500/Panacea''s how to run section to see additional actions)}} - put the Peacemonger''s **PEACETIME** reminder in center of the left side of the Grimoire.","At dusk, the Peacemonger''s protection will end if it''s active - remove the Peacemonger''s **PEACETIME** reminder token, **the Peacemonger loses their ability** - mark them with the **NO ABILITY** reminder and remove their night token from the night sheet {{i|(the Peacemonger won''t wake again)}}."],"quote":"This content feeling is nice and all, but the doves might be a problem.","iconBy":"le_nuberto","jinxes":[{"name":"Leviathan","align":"evil","text":"The Peacemonger''s ability activates if no one died was ''about to die'' today.","id":"leviathan"},{"name":"Riot","align":"evil","text":"If no good player nominates during the day, the Peacemonger''s ability will activate, even if they died today.","id":"riot"},{"name":"Matsuraid","align":"evil","text":"If the Matsuraid is in play and no good player nominates, the Peacemonger''s ability will activate.","id":"matsuraid_hblreleased"},{"name":"Au’Wre","align":"evil","text":"The Peacemonger''s ability activates if no one was ''about to die'' today.","id":"auwre_the_bootleggers_anthology"},{"name":"Ketos","align":"evil","text":"The Peacemonger''s ability activates if no one was ''about to die'' today.","id":"ketos_the_bootleggers_anthology"}],"customBoxes":[{"title":"In the almanac JSON","content":"**Reminders:** Harmonious, Harmonious, Harmonious, Harmonious, Harmonious, Peacetime, No ability"},{"title":"Alternative JSON & How to Run","content":"For if you feel like you want the ''Peace'' in ''Peacemonger'' should be more socially connected than mechanically connected, use this JSON. This introduces a new playstyle where the Peacemonger wants to confirm good players and protect a lot at once via asking the Town to hold off on an execution.\n\nEach night, wake the Peacemonger and have them choose a player. If they choose a player on their team, put a HARMONIOUS reminder token next to that player. Put the Peacemonger to sleep.\n\nEach dusk, if no player was executed today and the Peacemonger isn''t marked with the NO ABILITY reminder, all players marked with the Peacemonger''s HARMONIOUS reminder token are protected from all negative effects, including death, drunkenness, poisoning, or being turned evil (see SCP-500/Panacea''s how to run section to see additional actions) - place the Peacemonger''s PEACETIME reminder in center of the left side of the Grimoire. This no longer occurs at night if no one died by the time the Peacemonger would''ve woken up, and the Peacemonger loses their ability - mark them with the NO ABILITY reminder and remove their night token from the night sheet (the Peacemonger won''t wake again).\n\nAt dusk, the Peacemonger''s protection will end if it''s active - remove the Peacemonger''s PEACETIME reminder token.\n\n**Peacemonger █~** (Townsfolk)\nEach night, choose a player. The 1st time no one is executed, you & all chosen teammates are safe from everything until dusk.\n\n**First night:** The Peacemonger chooses a player. If a teammate is chosen, mark that player ''Chosen''.\n**Other nights:** The Peacemonger chooses a player. If a teammate is chosen, mark that player ''Chosen''. If no one is dieing tonight and the Peacemonger isn''t marked with ''No ability'': mark the Peacemonger with ''Peacetime''.\n**Reminders:** Harmonious, Harmonious, Harmonious, Harmonious, Harmonious, Peacetime, No ability\n**Credit:** Ability: @legitch. Image: @le_nuberto\n\n**Jinxes:**\nLeviathan: The Peacemonger''s ability activates only if no one died was ''about to die'' today.\nRiot: If no good player nominates during the day, the Peacemonger''s ability will activate, even if they died today.\nMatsuraid: If the Matsuraid is in play and no good player nominates, the Peacemonger''s ability will activate.\nAu’Wre: The Peacemonger''s ability activates only if no one was ''about to die'' today.\nKetos: The Peacemonger''s ability activates only if no one was ''about to die'' today."}],"firstNight":22.514,"otherNight":70.514,"reminders":["Harmonious","Harmonious","Harmonious","Harmonious","Harmonious","Harmonious","Harmonious","Harmonious","Peacetime","No ability"],"setup":false,"firstNightReminder":"The Peacemonger chooses a player. If a teammate is chosen, mark that player ''Chosen''.","otherNightReminder":"The Peacemonger chooses a player. If a teammate is chosen, mark that player ''Chosen''. If no one is dieing tonight and the Peacemonger isn''t marked with ''No ability'': mark the Peacemonger with ''Peacetime''.","art":"art/peacemonger-scp-fragmented-veil.png","jsonId":"peacemonger_scp_fragmented_veil","curata":false}','scp-fragmented-veil/peacemonger','published',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('desire-reader','Desire Reader','townsfolk','legitch',NULL,'','SCP Fragmented Veil','{"slug":"desire-reader","name":"Desire Reader","team":"townsfolk","ability":"Each day, privately choose a player: learn a trait they share with the previous player. You are sober & healthy only if they are.","creator":"legitch","appearsIn":"SCP Fragmented Veil","lede":"The Desire Reader (SCP-978) is a camera that can peer into the minds of others through the photographs it makes of those targets, revealing their souls.","summaryBullets":["Each day, the Desire Reader chooses a player to compare with the previously chosen player.","They can learn any fact provided that it relates to something both players share, such as an ability trait, or what they did at night.","The Desire Reader learns nothing on the first day","It is up to the Desire Reader to talk with the Storyteller, not the other way around. This isn''t a public conversation, and the group can''t listen in. It''s private.","The Desire Reader can choose not to visit the Storyteller if they wish.","The Desire Reader is normally sober and healthy, even if another ability targeted at the Desire Reader would make them drunk or poisoned.","However, if the Desire Reader chooses a drunk or poisoned player with their ability, they will be under drunk and poisoned behaviour, and will receive arbitrary information with their ability for that use.","The Desire Reader can choose themselves if they freely wish, and the Storyteller may give weaker information as a result."],"howToRun":["Once per day, if the Desire Reader requests a private chat with you, take them away from the circle so you cannot be overheard. They will choose a player. If there is a player marked with the **PREVIOUS** reminder token, whisper a fact about a commonality they share to the Desire Reader. Mark the chosen player with the **PREVIOUS** reminder token. Note that the Desire Reader is not affected by drunkenness and poisoning normally, but will receive arbitrary results should the player they select be, if so, mark them with the **DROISONED** reminder token until they choose a sober & healthy player again. If you cannot think of a thought-read straight away, either take your time or ask them to come back in a few minutes."],"tips":["Remember, the Desire Reader will be unaffected by conventional sources of drunkenness and poisoning unless their most recent choice was drunk or poisoned. This means that you should be cautious with how you tune the information you give to the Desire Reader each day. Try and aim for information that''s on par with an ''Each night/each night*'' Townsfolk''s ability."],"quote":"See foe''s remaining HP. Press [A Button](https://mario.wiki.gallery/images/b/b9/Switch_A_Button.svg) for secrets!","iconBy":"le_nuberto","jinxes":[{"name":"No Dashii","align":"evil","text":"The No Dashii''s poison skips over the Desire Reader.","id":"nodashii"},{"name":"Caruncula","align":"evil","text":"The Caruncula''s poison skips over the Desire Reader.","slug":"caruncula"},{"name":"Autarch","align":"evil","text":"The Desire Reader can normally be poisoned by the Autarch.","id":"autarch_hblreleased"}],"customBoxes":[{"title":"Alternative JSON (Older)","content":"If you feel like using the older Desire Reader where it ambiguously learned what a player is \"thinking\" at the present moment, use this JSON. Good for more casual and groups that prioritize having fun more than winning, but may not necessarily be better than the current text.\n\n**Desire Reader █~** (Townsfolk)\nEach day, privately choose a player: learn what they are \"thinking\".\n\n**Reminders:** Droisoned, Previous\n**Credit:** Ability: @legitch. Image: @le_nuberto."}],"firstNight":0,"otherNight":0,"reminders":["Droisoned","Previous"],"setup":false,"art":"art/desire-reader.png","jsonId":"desirereader_scp_fragmented_veil","curata":false}','scp-fragmented-veil/desire-reader','published',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('man-egg','MAN EGG™','townsfolk','legitch',NULL,'','SCP Fragmented Veil','{"slug":"man-egg","name":"MAN EGG™","team":"townsfolk","ability":"Once per game, during the day, visit the Storyteller to gain the ability your team needs (learn what it is).","creator":"legitch","appearsIn":"SCP Fragmented Veil","lede":"The MAN EGG™ (SCP-1657) is exactly what the team needs. They''re more accurate with landing a crucial ability the longer they cook and abstain from acting.","summaryBullets":["The Storyteller decides what the MAN EGG™''s ability is when they call for it. It may be the same ability as another character in Blood On The Clocktower, something similar, or something original.","The MAN EGG™ may wake at any time during the night to learn information or to choose a player, or their ability may be passive - not requiring action from them. Regardless, the MAN EGG™ knows exactly what their ability is.","If the MAN EGG™ used their ability while drunk or poisoned, they will still be told they got their ability, but they never actually did, and thus will be drunk/poisoned indefinitely."],"howToRun":["At any time during the day, the MAN EGG™ can approach the Storyteller if they aren''t marked with the **HATCHED** reminder and privately to gain a new ability. The Storyteller writes down this ability on a piece of paper, or on a phone, then lets the MAN EGG™ know what it is. Mark them with the **HATCHED** reminder.","During the game, treat that player as if they had that ability, waking them when needed, prompting them to choose players when needed, or whatever else is appropriate. Use the MAN EGG™’s **?** reminders if you need to."],"tips":["It''s generally recommended that when you grant the MAN EGG™ their ability, it aims towards something similar to an existing or homebrew Blood on the Clocktower character, but given some improvements based on how long the MAN EGG™ was willing to hold off on using their ability."],"quote":"\"The longer you wait, the stronger it is!™\" -MAN EGG","iconBy":"le_nuberto","jinxes":[{"name":"Vortox","align":"evil","text":"The MAN EGG™ knowing their ability is not effected by the Vortox.","id":"vortox"},{"name":"Disruptor","align":"evil","text":"The MAN EGG™ knowing their ability is not effected by the Disruptor.","slug":"disruptor"},{"name":"Miasma","align":"evil","text":"The MAN EGG™ knowing their ability is not effected by the Miasma.","id":"miasma_the_bootleggers_anthology"},{"name":"Muñoz","align":"good","text":"The Muñoz thinking they''re a MAN EGG™ does not have false information affect knowing what their ability is.","id":"munoz_2tfafullcharacterlist"},{"name":"Charlatan","align":"evil","text":"The MAN EGG™ knowing their ability is not effected by the Charlatan.","id":"charlatan_2tfafullcharacterlist"},{"name":"Visitor","align":"good","text":"The MAN EGG™ knowing their ability is not effected by the Visitor.","id":"visitor_2tfafullcharacterlist"},{"name":"Absolut","align":"evil","text":"The MAN EGG™ knowing their ability is not effected by the Absolut.","id":"absolut"}],"firstNight":0,"otherNight":0,"reminders":["?","?","?","Hatched"],"setup":false,"art":"art/man-egg.png","jsonId":"manegg_scp_fragmented_veil","curata":false}','scp-fragmented-veil/man-egg','published',datetime('now'),datetime('now')),
('hangman-scp-fragmented-veil','Hangman','townsfolk','legitch',NULL,'','SCP Fragmented Veil','{"slug":"hangman-scp-fragmented-veil","name":"Hangman","team":"townsfolk","ability":"You can''t die at night. Each night, choose a unique letter: learn how many evil''s names have it. If 0 for Minions, you are drunk.","creator":"legitch","appearsIn":"SCP Fragmented Veil","lede":"SCP-2121 is an infinitely hanging rope that allows communication with divine forces to learn answers, at the risk of the user''s own life.","summaryBullets":["The Hangman has already been hanged... so to speak. They cannot die at night, but may are still vulnerable during the day.","Each night, the Hangman takes a shot at a alphabetical letter, and learns how many evil players have at-least 1 of it in their character''s names.","The Hangman is not allowed to pick a symbol, number, or repeat letter {{i|(unless the Storyteller decides otherwise for the first two this game.)}}","If the Hangman''s result is 0 specifically for Minions, the Hangman henceforth is drunk, and will receive arbitrary results and can die at night."],"howToRun":["Each night, wake the Hangman. They point at a letter on the script, or otherwise indicate a letter to the Storyteller silently. If 0 evil Minions have this letter in their name, the Hangman is **drunk** - mark them with the **DRUNK** reminder token. Then, show them fingers {{i|(0, 1, 2, etc.)}} equalling the number of evil players with at-least one of those letters in their name. Put the Hangman to sleep.","If the sober Hangman would die at night, the Hangman remains alive."],"tips":["When creating scripts using the Hangman, be very mindful of what Minions and Demons you are adding in order to create a fun experience for the Hangman - otherwise, don''t include them. It''s best recommended to put the Hangman on scripts with at least 5 Minions."],"quote":"How''s it hangin''?","iconBy":"le_nuberto","jinxes":[{"name":"Legion","align":"evil","text":"If the Legion is in-play, the Hangman instead learns how many in-play good characters'' names have that letter instead of in-play evil characters'' names, with Townsfolk registering as Minions here.","id":"legion"},{"name":"Daivout","align":"good","text":"If the Daivout is in-play & most players are the Daivout, the Hangman instead learns how many in-play good characters'' names have that letter instead of in-play evil characters'' names, with Townsfolk registering as Minions here.","id":"daivout_darkartists_stuff"}],"customBoxes":[{"title":"Alternative JSON & How to Run (Older)","content":"Once per day, if the Hangman requests a private chat with you, take them away from the circle so you cannot be overheard. They will tell you a letter/character. Whisper them the number of how many in-play evil character''s names have at least 1 of these in their name. If there are 0 Minions with it, **they might die tonight** ***(even if the Hangman was made to learn a different number instead of the truth)*** - mark them with the **MIGHT DIE** reminder.\n\nAt night, if the Hangman is marked with the **MIGHT DEAD** reminder, you may choose that the Hangman {{i|dies}} - mark them with the **DEAD** reminder.\n\n**Hangman █** (Townsfolk)\nEach day, privately choose a letter: Learn how many evil character''s names have it. If it''s 0 for Minions, you might die tonight.\n\n**Other nights:** If the Hangman''s chose a letter where no Minions had it in their name today: the Hangman might die.\n**Reminders:** Might die, Dead\n**Credit:** Ability: @legitch. Image: @le_nuberto\n\n**Jinxes:**\nLegion: If the Legion is in-play, the Hangman instead learns how many in-play good characters'' names have that letter instead of in-play evil characters'' names, with Townsfolk registering as Minions here.\nDaivout: If the Daivout is in-play & most players are the Daivout, the Hangman instead learns how many in-play good characters'' names have that letter instead of in-play evil characters'' names, with Townsfolk registering as Minions here."}],"firstNight":18.2121,"otherNight":3.2121,"reminders":["Drunk"],"setup":false,"firstNightReminder":"The Hangman chooses a new letter. Show the hand signal for the number (0, 1, 2, etc.) of evil players who have at-least 1 of that letter in their character''s name. If it''s 0 in regards to Minions specifically, the Hangman is drunk.","otherNightReminder":"The Hangman chooses a new letter. Show the hand signal for the number (0, 1, 2, etc.) of evil players who have at-least 1 of that letter in their character''s name. If it''s 0 in regards to Minions specifically, the Hangman is drunk.","art":"art/hangman-scp-fragmented-veil.png","jsonId":"hangman_scp_fragmented_veil","curata":false}','scp-fragmented-veil/hangman','published',datetime('now'),datetime('now'));
